<title>USA: Brent crude steady in thin U.S. paper trading.</title>
<headline>Brent crude steady in thin U.S. paper trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Sea Brent crude oil was steady in thin U.S. paper trading on Tuesday afternoon, traders said.</p>
<p>Two August partial cargoes traded 100 times apiece at $18.36 and $18.40 a barrel.</p>
<p>London's IPE settled at $18.39 for August, up 19 cents from Monday.</p>
<p>July/August Brent changed hands at plus 25 cents a barrel, while August/September moved at minus eight cents.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
</text>
